            0.217
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.227,
            0.882,
            0.262
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q1. Do you see any line of symmetry in the figures at the start of the chapter? What about in the picture of the cloud?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.271,
            0.881,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. Yes, there are 6, 4 and 1 lines of symmetry in the figures of flower, rangoli and butterfly respectively. There is no line of symmetry in the figures of pinwheel and cloud."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.316,
            0.809,
            0.335
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q2. For each of the following figures, identify the line(s) of symmetry if it exists.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.345,
            0.162,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.507,
            0.216,
            0.524
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Section 9.1"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.534,
            0.232,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Page no. 221",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.561,
            0.881,
            0.598
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q. Is there any other way to fold the square so that the two halves overlap? How many lines of symmetry does the square shape have?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.607,
            0.521,
            0.625
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. No, there is no other way to fold the square."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.634,
            0.502,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The square shape has 4 lines of symmetry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.661,
            0.881,
            0.697
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q. We saw that the diagonal of a square is also a line of symmetry. Let us take a rectangle that is not a square. Is its diagonal a line of symmetry?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.706,
            0.582,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. No, Rectangle’s diagonal is not a line of symmetry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.76,
            0.233,
            0.778
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Page no. 222"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.788,
            0.881,
            0.824
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q. What if we reflect along the diagonal from A to C? Where do points A, B, C and D go? What if we reflect along the horizontal line of symmetry?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.833,
            0.881,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If we reflect along the diagonal from A to C, D occupies the position occupied by B earlier. A and C remain at the same place."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.877,
            0.882,
            0.913
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we reflect along the horizontal line of symmetry, D and C occupies the position earlier occupied by A and B respectively."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
